  "_note": "Fold-level standard errors for body Table 3 (tab:condition-modulation), slot-machine Ridge readout R^2 at L22 by prompt condition. METHOD: SE = fold_sd/sqrt(5) over the 5 GroupKFold-by-game folds -- the same definition Table 1 uses in paper_data/table1_se_N200.json. SOURCE: the released field 'r2_std' in sae_v3_analysis/results/condition_modulation_groupkfold_L22.json, the same file the printed point estimates come from; no re-fit was run. All 30 printed R^2 cells were first reproduced from that file to 3 dp with max deviation 0.000. EXCEPTION, 'All variable' row: it is Table 1's Gemma-SM / LLaMA-SM row re-printed (identical R^2, n and fold sd in the released files), so its SE is carried over from table1_se_N200.json rather than recomputed, and the two tables print the same +-. The two derivations agree to <=0.0007 in fold sd; they would differ in print for LLaMA SM I_LC and I_BA only (released 0.004 vs permutation-run 0.003), because table1_se_N200.json comes from the repo's independent permutation re-fit and this file comes from the released run. Both values are recorded per cell below. DELTA ROWS: Delta_G% and Delta_M% are ratios of two of these R^2 means; with denominators as small as 0.008 +- 0.007 a percentage interval is uninformative, so none is printed. The well-defined object, the paired difference (+G minus -G, +M minus -M) with SE = sqrt(se_plus^2 + se_minus^2) -- the two arms are disjoint sets of games, so their folds are independent -- is recorded under 'delta_rows'. FIXED ROW: the values printed in the paper come from a different pipeline (condition_modulation_continuous_ilc_L22.json, plain CV), whose release stores no per-fold R^2, so no SE exists for the printed fixed row. The game-grouped counterparts already quoted in the table's dagger footnote do have fold sd, and their SEs are under 'fixed_row'.",
